Android's cRGalaxy::BoxOn (00058d80) titles a route card "%s: %s", the level's
numeral from gRomanNumbers (0x8c22c: "", I .. LI) before the galaxy name, so the
card is sized around it: "XVI: Planoribis rubrum". Postal and Pro share BoxOn. Its
layout loop also keeps the longer card on screen: a card that would start left of
40 is anchored at 50 and stays there (literals at 0x4918c-0x491a8). The PC keeps its
own right, top and bottom bounds.

